== Physical inventory and independent weights

The join keys full directed particle-labeled multigraphs, retaining each parallel edge and its vertex rule. Both producers have the same original source identities and exact weights:

- `GL0`: two `V_36` vertices and three parallel gluons; automorphism 12, no Grassmann loop, `+1/12`.
- `GL1`: two `V_35` ghost-gluon vertices and a directed ghost circuit; automorphism 2, one Grassmann loop, `-1/2`.
- `GL2`: two `V_135` u-gluon vertices and a directed u circuit; automorphism 2, one Grassmann loop, `-1/2`.
- `GL3`: two `V_137` top-gluon vertices and a directed top circuit; automorphism 2, one Grassmann loop, `-1/2`.
- `GL4`: two `V_74` d-gluon vertices and a directed d circuit; automorphism 2, one Grassmann loop, `-1/2`.
- `GL5`: one `V_37` four-gluon vertex and two undirected self loops; automorphism 8, no Grassmann loop, `+1/8`.

The independent automorphism calculation counts vertex permutations and parallel-edge permutations while respecting direction. For `GL0`, `3! * 2 = 12`. Each directed circuit permits the two-vertex exchange but no directed edge flip. For `GL5`, its two self-loop endpoint flips and loop exchange give `2^2 * 2 = 8`. The graph-derived Grassmann parity requires one incoming and one outgoing anticommuting carrier at every occupied vacuum vertex, follows each closed directed component, and reproduces every actual `InternalFermionLoopSign` head and exact rational weight. This calculation uses the live ghost graph and model, not the separate photon/top-pair case.

`GL5` is the only graph excluded by the nonfactorizable filter. The grouped all-graphs row has six raw members, five final graphs, singleton constant `1/8+1/12-1/2-1/2 = -19/24`, and exact total `-43/24`. The nonfactorizable row has five raw members, four final graphs, singleton constant `1/12-1/2-1/2 = -11/12`, and exact total `-23/12`. Its obsolete `+1/12` singleton constant would arise from counting the actual ghost loop as `+1/2`; the correct closed-loop sign changes that constant by exactly `-1`.

The only repeated mass/spin topology is the u/d pair. Both native group inventories select `GL4` as master, bind source IDs 4 and 2 to their original named physical graphs, and store ratios `1,1`. The final factor contains exactly `NumeratorDependentGrouping(2,1,-1/2)` and `NumeratorDependentGrouping(4,1,-1/2)`. Thus the actual current all-graphs summary is `5 | -19/24+Group(2,1,-1/2)+Group(4,1,-1/2) = -43/24`, and the nonfactorizable summary is `4 | -11/12+Group(2,1,-1/2)+Group(4,1,-1/2) = -23/12`. Source43 produces those same summaries. These identities, not a normalized Group string, determine the labels.

